generate|produce|VERB|cause something to be produced|To produce something or cause it to come into existence.|tạo ra; phát sinh|The workshop generated several ideas for improving the playground.|Buổi hội thảo tạo ra một số ý tưởng để cải thiện sân chơi.|Transitive; objects may be ideas, income, energy, or other results, depending on context.|0
legislative|law-making|ADJECTIVE|relating to making laws|Relating to the process or bodies responsible for making laws.|thuộc lập pháp; liên quan đến việc làm luật|The committee examined the legislative process in its civics lesson.|Ủy ban xem xét quy trình lập pháp trong buổi học về công dân.|Usually before a noun such as process, body, or power; distinguish law-making from enforcing existing law.|0
protection|keeping-safe|NOUN|action or condition of keeping safe|The act of keeping someone or something safe from harm, or the safety provided.|sự bảo vệ; sự che chở|The cover gives the equipment protection from dust.|Tấm phủ bảo vệ thiết bị khỏi bụi.|Usually uncountable; protection from or against names the possible harm.|0
testing|checking-performance|NOUN|process of checking quality or operation|The process of checking how something works or whether it meets a requirement.|việc kiểm tra; việc kiểm nghiệm|Testing revealed that one of the lights did not work.|Việc kiểm tra cho thấy một trong các đèn không hoạt động.|Uncountable process noun; testing of something names the item being checked.|0
withdraw|take-money-out|VERB|take money from an account|To take money out of an account or financial arrangement.|rút tiền|She withdrew enough cash to pay for the bus tickets.|Cô ấy rút đủ tiền mặt để trả tiền vé xe buýt.|Transitive withdraw money from an account; past withdrew and past participle withdrawn.|0
withdraw|leave|VERB|leave an activity or position|To stop taking part in something or move away from a place or position.|rút khỏi; rút lui|The team withdrew from the competition after its captain became ill.|Đội rút khỏi cuộc thi sau khi đội trưởng bị ốm.|Intransitive withdraw from an activity; transitive withdraw a team removes it from participation.|1
withdraw|take-back|VERB|take back a statement or offer|To formally take back something previously said, offered, or submitted.|rút lại|The applicant withdrew her request before the meeting.|Người nộp đơn rút lại yêu cầu trước cuộc họp.|Transitive with objects such as a request, statement, or offer; does not necessarily imply the original was false.|2
